<urn:usf:future-use-pattern-catalogue:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Containing a pattern is not selecting it. A product must select a pattern explicitly through its own experience profile; nothing is inherited by being in this catalogue." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern-catalogue:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Five patterns are declared because this catalogue's first consumer selects exactly five. A larger speculative set would look like authority while never having been exercised by a real journey." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern-catalogue:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Reusable interaction patterns any USF product may select. A pattern says what must be experienced; it never says how, in what framework, or for which product." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern-catalogue:1> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:semantic-model> <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
