<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:assistiveSemantics> "The input is marked invalid programmatically and the reason is associated with it, so it is announced when the input is reached rather than only visible." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "validation-feedback" <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:focusBehaviour> "Focus is not moved away from the input when it becomes invalid; the actor is mid-correction." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:keyboardBehaviour> "The reason is reachable from the input by keyboard without leaving the field." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:patternAnatomy> "An association between the reason and the input it concerns." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:patternAnatomy> "The specific reason, in the actor's terms rather than the system's." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:patternPurpose> "Tell someone precisely why what they supplied cannot be used, next to what they supplied, while it can still be corrected." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:prohibitedShortcut> "Do not report invalidity only on submit when it was knowable earlier." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:prohibitedShortcut> "Do not state that something is invalid without stating why." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
<urn:usf:future-use-pattern:validation-feedback:1> <urn:usf:predicate:prohibitedShortcut> "Do not use colour as the only signal of invalidity." <urn:usf:graph:future-use-patterns> .
